From: Uke Linux contributors <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: llcc: skip the absent Cliffs7 broadcast-AND window

The admitted Cliffs7 profile has exactly four bank apertures and one
broadcast aperture. Probing a sixth resource emits -EINVAL even though
the driver already supports polling through the broadcast window.

Skip that optional mapping for the validated SM7675 profile. Keep the
existing error handling and resource policy for other platforms. The
host probe test rejects any sixth access and retains write-fault,
activation-fault, resource, version and unrelated-SCID checks.

Source: MiCode Uke DT 94c84aeb9e517dbde546fc732033c184094c8e57,
qcom/cliffs.dtsi, cache-controller@25000000; kernel5712080a, LLCC v5
broadcast fallback. No cache policy or register value changes.

Signed-off-by: Uke Linux contributors <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/llcc-qcom.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/llcc-qcom.c
index ad23626..0fa936b 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/llcc-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/llcc-qcom.c
@@ -5752,8 +5752,8 @@ static int qcom_llcc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		goto err;
 	}
 
-	/* Applicable only when drv_data->version >= 4.1 */
-	if (drv_data->version >= LLCC_VERSION_4_1_0_0) {
+	/* Cliffs7 has no broadcast-AND window; its five resources were checked. */
+	if (drv_data->version >= LLCC_VERSION_4_1_0_0 && !sm7675) {
 		drv_data->bcast_and_regmap = qcom_llcc_init_mmio(pdev, i + 1, "llcc_broadcast_and_base");
 		if (IS_ERR(drv_data->bcast_and_regmap)) {
 			ret = PTR_ERR(drv_data->bcast_and_regmap);
